6️⃣ Latency vs Throughput
Latency

Delay

Time for a packet to travel

Measured in ms

Example:

“How fast does the first byte arrive?”

Throughput

Capacity

Data transferred per second

Measured in Mbps / Gbps

Example:

“How much data can flow continuously?”

🚗 Analogy:

Latency = time for car to reach highway

Throughput = number of cars per hour

7️⃣ CDN (Origin vs Edge, Cache Hit/Miss)
Origin Server

Main backend server

Source of truth

Edge Server

Located close to users

Caches content

Cache Hit

Content served from edge

Fast

Low latency

Cheaper

Cache Miss

Edge asks origin

Slower

Then caches response

💡 Interview line:

“CDNs reduce latency, offload origin servers, and improve scalability.”

